#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:51
#: 031ed18daeae45de88e6394f9ad1c5e3
msgid "Airframe: X-UAV MiniTalon RC Plane Kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:52
#: 506c8b74cbe0495b8f3e993dcb23c078
msgid "Motor: Cobra 2221-16 940KV or SunnySky 2216 1450KV"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:53
#: 57b896a627dc40c69ff2f6adadd22380
msgid "ESC: 40-60A, no BEC required"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:54
#: bdc8319ff79b453bae30eb9fe2e7d66e
msgid "Prop: APC-E or Aeronaut folding 9X7 for Cobra, 8x6 for Sunnysky motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:55
#: bd7ec61c29274a1582882eba3bee72b8
msgid "Servos: 4- 9g to 12g mini servos. EMAX ES08MA, for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:56
#: 4ca3b818cede4a82b9f5ff3a6cfd2310
msgid "Autopilot: MatekF405-Wing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:57
#: bf919462cc4f4a7ebedfd3068d09d0b0
msgid "GPS: Any UBLOX MN-8 class GPS with or without compass (Compass is optional). BN-220 is an example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:58
#: e6e12c5509264c5cb291222555295601
msgid "Receiver: Any 6 Channel TX/RX system. For long range, 433 or 900 Mhz systems (Dragonlink, TBS, etc.) are appropriate, short range 2.4GHz (FRSky, Futaba, Spektrum,etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:59
#: 61005cbb1e914b1e85260259c29aa879
msgid "Telemetry (optional): 3DR or  radio systems, or via the receiver if it has that capability, like Dragonlink (bi-directional) or FRSky (downlink only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:60
#: f49b54435fea4af9b525e52b75c1f7ec
msgid "Battery: A 4s 5200mah 10C Lipo will give 45-60 minute duration and fit the general layout for easy CG (Center-of-Gravity) placement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:61
#: 70bec105393f4839a057e843a379fdbf
msgid "FPV Equipment: A miniature video camera and video transmitter are required (if FPV capability is desired, the plane can be flown only line-of-sight, and still fly autonomous missions using a GCS (ground control station) only, if desired. See FPV Equipment section below for suggestions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:64
#: 7f7b71546ab245868637a71dec6429c3
msgid "Assembly Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:66
#: e97b654964cb4c628f54d74448cd00b3
msgid "The instructions for building the MiniTalon are straightforward, however, a few tips are shown below that will help."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:69
#: f00d460ccb3d44a5ac15d4d5e8065ec3
msgid "Fuse Prep & Glue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:71
#: 6a83d2b1c90c4279a485b089c06092fa
msgid "For gluing EPO foam, use Beacon Foam-Tac or E6000 which works very well and it sets fairly quickly. To prepare the pieces, always wash all surfaces of all parts in hot water with a small amount of dish soap to get rid of any mold release agents. Next, do a wipe down with denatured alcohol and finally a light sand on the glue surfaces with #100 grit sandpaper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:73
#: 64098ec5c6eb429f818e5a8cd7d61f88
msgid "Before gluing the fuselage halves, set up the motor mount plate with APC prop bushings and 3mm blind nuts to get the motor off the wood for better cooling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:84
#: 36aded13c76449b8932d97edfad2b475
msgid "After gluing in the motor mount, glue in the center structure. Optionally, add some cable guides to each side and some velcro lock to hold the Receiver. The center structure does not come with a floor in the kit to allow mounting the autopilot. Either add a ply plate to the bottom, or 3D print one of Mark Qvale's mounting plates from his `website <https://itsqv.com>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:93
#: 57c78c4d0d1248e7a6453f0e22dd74fb
msgid "Optional Front Skid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:95
#: 73c8c5067e514111bbb62aa5675f01a6
msgid "The kit comes with a front wheel. This breaks quickly, so it's suggested that it not be used. Either tape the area with re-enforced packing tape or 3D print or fabricate a ply skid as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:100
#: f91c1803ef2c425483f78e7582c87328
msgid "Coating the tail skid with re-enforced tape will also increase its life."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:103
#: 39e2fdd7347d4bbbaf110197d7469add
msgid "Vtail Servo Linkage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:105
#: 15e457882e57499fab5d9004e3c3cf54
msgid "The provides straight pushrods to the Vtail surfaces. However, there is high miss-alignment caused by the stock geometry which puts the linkage at an angle to the control surface. The linkage, as provided will work reliably, however, to reduce strain and any possibility of wear, you can use a ball-link as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:111
#: 1f2299a0590a49779fa4507b66333ac1
msgid "Power Train"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:113
#: 7a1aa7fbc163401891c74a8f2fdf8753
msgid "It's important to keep the leads from the autopilot's ESC power terminals short (<4-5inchs)to the ESC. If long leads are unavoidable, you will need to add low-ESR capacitors to the ESC input to prevent possible damage. Some ESCs already have these capacitors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:115
#: 488dcb8db9154a87823097926ab1ff12
msgid "Long leads from the ESC to the motor are acceptable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:117
#: 553c6c2baf264422b455d010ab27e5e2
msgid "Increased efficiency will be obtained if the ESC is programmed to brake hard when gliding. A folding propeller also helps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:120
#: b97423e6ec32480b8f2b1d1747b0fcb2
msgid "Folding Prop Stopper"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:122
#: 7f8f2cd575e2418b8b8dd8cc037b9b27
msgid "If an Aeronaut or other folding prop is used to improve efficiency, it will require a prop stopper. A 3d printed design is available on Mark Qvale's `website <https://itsqv.com>`_."
msgstr ""

