msgid ":ref:`SERVO1_FUNCTION<SERVO1_FUNCTION>`   |  Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:148
#: 469e69b4c2884b2a866c9d71f6055a67
msgid ":ref:`SERVO3_FUNCTION<SERVO3_FUNCTION>`   |  Both Ailerons via Y-servo cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:150
#: 05c8dcd187b148d8afe5828a2880c094
msgid ":ref:`SERVO4_FUNCTION<SERVO4_FUNCTION>`   |  VTail Left"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:152
#: cbf1eda7da814c12ae5c01904d3ad45a
msgid ":ref:`SERVO5_FUNCTION<SERVO5_FUNCTION>`   |  VTail Right"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:155
#: 934b489ff2884d4cb717f27f7d95a6b8
msgid "If the aileron servos are  attached to separate PWM outputs the :ref:`flaperons<flaperons-on-plane>` function can be implemented. However, since the MiniTalon does not use full length ailerons, the flap effect will be limited and can even be detrimental, causing increased sensitivity to \"tip stalls\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:157
#: a0fe6f72e5554b7e9bd60dbe53db141c
msgid "If an LRS (Long Range RC System) is utilized, mounting the antenna is critical to achieving maximum distance. Most LRS systems use a dipole. Shown below is a 3d printed mount that assures that both elements are vertical. Any method that assures that the dipole is mounted vertically will be satisfactory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:166
#: 1188b3c41e7543b399c2f14820c0cab6
msgid "Configuration/Parameter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:168
#: 327d82efb47442bba39a1b9181e74ce1
msgid "See :ref:`FPV Plane <basic-setup>` for information on software setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:171
#: 95ea44a8d287411699794b2cd1e01ae0
msgid "FPV Equipment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:173
#: ead7fbe445ff41079fdb2046d4879b83
msgid "Choices for FPV cameras and transmitters are numerous and increase daily. Be sure that both camera and video transmitter can operate at 9V, since the MatekF405-Wing autopilot provides this supply for video. Optionally, the video supply can be changed from 9V to 12V via a solder jumper on the back of the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:175
#: f330b1f06ccc4850912809f89a032bdf
msgid "For long range operation, the video transmitter should operate on 1.2Ghz or 1.3Ghz . For distances of 2Km or less, 5.8GHz transmission is usually used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:177
#: 4364c4a4db314ffb979acd48abcb5628
msgid "No external OSD (On Screen Display) is required since the MatekF405-Wing has it integrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:179
#: 5110fcfb81294ad7a09d36dc539e8c84
msgid "See the :ref:`FPV information page <common-fpv-first-person-view>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:182
#: d62eb9563f3b4068a67a0185f66922c5
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:185
#: 335dde0833494c5d922d8d42c988ff5e
msgid "Airspeed Sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:187
#: 6953dea8f7d94febac810a738f10494e
msgid "With the addition of a digital airspeed sensor, precision airspeed control can be obtained during cruise portions of flight, and can be attached to the MatekF405-Wing autopilot's CL1/DA1 or CL2/DA2 pins. However, this is optional and ArduPlane flies extremely well without this addition. See the :ref:`Airspeed sensor <airspeed>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:196
#: 63d582e306a248bab9a0f0c028ec1e23
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:198
#: 65b0b5142fe64d5ea98cb596fba15765
msgid "Similarly, a compass can be added by attaching to the autopilot's CL1/DA1 or CL2/DA2 pins. This is also optional and provides marginally better navigation tracking in CRUISE and AUTO modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:202
#: 47aa842ee7e148488652d37d22d7fde4
msgid "Gimbles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:204
#: 575674fb2ddf4b2ba834c2c5174be422
msgid "Many options exist for mounting either an HD recording camera and/or the flight video camera to a pan/tilt controllable mount. In addition, these gimble mounts can even be stabilized in one or more axis. to provide cinema-like stability. Mark Qvale's `website <https://itsqv.com>`_ has many examples and versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/miniTalon-build.rst:206
#: 0662d55c30654822af4f34d1d697ed9d
msgid "It is usually not a good idea to have the flight camera mounted on a stabilized mount since the operator will lose the feedback of the plane's attitude while flying."
msgstr ""

